    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d948">

                <pb facs="0847" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2994.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-01T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1912—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I answered Department’s March 1, 5 p.m., in my February 29, 7 p.m.
                    Representations were made several days ago, and the best information I have now
                    is that a military force is at Velardena and found the Americans all well.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
